      { question: "Why is my state wrong near a border?", answer: "State lines are digitized in GIS databases with finite precision. Within a few hundred meters of a border, your device's accuracy radius may straddle the line and return the neighboring state." },
      { question: "Can I check when I cross a state line?", answer: "Yes. Keep this page open while traveling and press the refresh button — each new fix re-resolves your position and updates the state the moment you cross." },
      { question: "Is state detection available worldwide?", answer: "Almost. Any country with digitized first-level administrative boundaries works, which covers the vast majority. Very small nations may not have a state level at all." }
