      { question: "What format should I use to share my coordinates?", answer: "Decimal degrees (e.g., 40.7128, -74.0060) is the most universal — it works in Google Maps, Apple Maps, and most apps. Use DMS only when a document or instrument specifically asks for it." },
      { question: "How many decimal places do I need?", answer: "Four decimals (~11 m) is enough to describe a building; six decimals (~0.1 m) exceeds what consumer GPS can actually measure. Extra digits add precision on paper, not in reality." },
      { question: "Why do my coordinates change slightly while I stand still?", answer: "Satellite signals, atmospheric conditions, and multipath reflections cause small fluctuations of a few meters. That's normal — the accuracy circle shows the range your true position likely falls in." }
